# DianaSh golden corpus. Recorded from the C# shell, byte for byte, and frozen since its recorder went with the C# core host on 2026-11-07 - see EmuSen_DianaSh.md §13.4.
# Patterns: <ROOT> is the sandbox's real root, <TEMP> the corpus's real temporary folder, <INSTALL> the install's real directory;
# a 'match' block is a regular expression the whole output must match, written where a line prints a time or a measured number.
command cheat
usage 1   cheat add <code> [description]    decode a code, guessing whether it's Pro
usage 2                                      Action Replay/Game Wizard or Game Genie from
usage 3                                      its formatting (see `gg` if it guesses wrong -
usage 4                                      both formats use the same 8 hex-digit
usage 5                                      characters, so this is a best-effort guess,
usage 6                                      not a guarantee)
usage 7   cheat poke <space> <addr> <value> [description] [-w 1|2|4] [--le|--be] [--dec|--float] [--json]
usage 8                                      add a raw RAM-poke cheat directly, bypassing
usage 9                                      code decoding (e.g. an address you already
usage 10                                     found with `search`)
usage 11  cheat from-freeze <id> [--keep|--remove] [--json] [description]
usage 12                                     graduate an active freeze into a persisted
usage 13                                     custom cheat
usage 14  cheat gg <code> [description]     decode a real SNES Game Genie code (8
usage 15                                     characters) and add it as a ROM patch, enabled
usage 16                                     - use this instead of `add` when its guess is
usage 17                                     wrong for a code formatted unconventionally
usage 18  cheat rompatch <addr> <value> [<compare>|-] [description]
usage 19                                     add a Game Genie-style ROM-read intercept
usage 20                                     directly, bypassing code decoding: substitute
usage 21                                     <value> for reads of cartridge address <addr>.
usage 22                                     <compare> gates the patch to only apply while
usage 23                                     the real byte there equals it (pass - to skip,
usage 24                                     an unconditional patch - what every real SNES
usage 25                                     Game Genie code decodes to; unlike NES/Genesis,
usage 26                                     SNES Game Genie codes never carry a compare)
usage 27  cheat list [--json]                list every cheat with its ID, kind, and state
usage 28  cheat master [on|off]              one switch over every cheat at once, without
usage 29                                     touching any cheat's own enabled state (no
usage 30                                     argument reports which way it is set)
usage 31  cheat enable <id>                  turn a cheat back on
usage 32  cheat disable <id>                 turn a cheat off without removing it
usage 33  cheat remove <id>                  remove a cheat entirely
usage 34  cheat clear                        remove every cheat
usage 35  cheat save <name>                  write every cheat to
usage 36                                     /etc/EmuSen/cheats/<name>.json
usage 37  cheat load <name>                  add every cheat from that file to whatever
usage 38                                     is already loaded (`cheat clear` first to
usage 39                                     replace rather than merge)
usage 40  cheat files                        list the saved cheat files
usage 41  cheat import <path.cht>            import RetroArch/libretro .cht cheats, added
usage 42                                     disabled so nothing turns on by surprise
usage 43  cheat export <path.cht>            write RAM-poke cheats out as a .cht file
usage 44  cheat db [status]                  where the cheat database is, and what is in it
usage 45  cheat db find <game>               search the database for a game
usage 46  cheat db load <game>               import that game's cheats, disabled
usage 47  cheat db update                    download the libretro cheat database (CC BY-SA 4.0)
usage 48  cheat db prune [--apply]           delete the systems no core in this build can use
uncovered 47 -- it downloads the libretro database over the network, which the corpus does not reach

case with no target
target none
covers 1
$ cheat list
out 65
Error: No ROM loaded - this command needs an active debug target.
status 1
action none
$ echo $?
out 1
1
status 0
action none
end

